==English==

===Etymology===
From {{suf|en|tear|ful|pos=adjective}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪə(ɹ)fʊl/|/ˈtɪə(ɹ)fəl/}}
* {{a|GA}} {{IPA|en|/ˈtɪɹfʊl/|/ˈtɪɹfəl/}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɪə(ɹ)fʊl|ɪɹfʊl|ɪə(ɹ)fəl|ɪɹfəl|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj}}

# Accompanied by [[tear]]s; [[crying]], or about to [[cry]].
#: ''Aaron was a little '''tearful''' until Laura came to reassure him.''
# [[sorrowful|Sorrowful]].
#: {{syn|en|lachrymose}}

